From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] parser: report argument types when overload resolution fails

"no instance of overloaded function 'f' matches the argument list" did not
say what the argument list was, which makes a kernel build failure very hard
to diagnose -- the type errors fixed by the preceding patches were all found
by adding this.

List the actual argument types in the message. The neighbouring catch block
did print them, but to stderr, along with a dump of every candidate overload;
fold that into the reported error instead so the information reaches whoever
called clBuildProgram.
---
--- a/src/parser/parser.cpp
+++ b/src/parser/parser.cpp
@@ -1963,7 +1963,12 @@
 						{
 							const smartptr<callable> &fn = overloaded->get_function(arg_types);
 							if (!fn)
-								ERROR("no instance of overloaded function '" + overloaded->get_name() + "' matches the argument list");
+							{
+								std::string __a;
+								for(size_t __i = 0 ; __i < arg_types.size() ; ++__i)
+									__a += (__i ? ", " : "") + (arg_types[__i] ? arg_types[__i]->get_name() : std::string("NULL"));
+								ERROR("no instance of overloaded function '" + overloaded->get_name() + "' matches the argument list (" + __a + ")");
+							}
 							exp = fn;
 						}
 
@@ -1999,10 +2004,8 @@
 								arg_list += arg_types[i]->get_name();
 							}
 							arg_list += ')';
-							std::cerr << arg_list << std::endl;
-							if (exp.as<overloaded_builtin>())
-								exp.as<overloaded_builtin>()->print_debug_info();
-							ERROR(e.what());
+							ERROR(std::string(e.what()) + "\nwhile calling '"
+								  + exp.as<callable>()->get_name() + arg_list + "'");
 						}
 
 						exp = new call(exp, args);
